---
// Terms: the few rules for using Yo (App Review Guideline 1.2).
import { operator, lastUpdated } from '../../data/legal';
---
<section id="terms" class="legal-section">
  <h2>Terms</h2>
  <p class="muted">Updated: {lastUpdated.terms}</p>


    <p>By using Yo you agree to these terms. Yo is run by {operator.name}, see the <a href="#imprint">imprint</a>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>No abuse of service.</b> Harassment, threats, hate, spam or anything illegal, in names, groups, photos
        or videos, will get your account blocked.</li>
      <li><b>Report and block.</b> Anyone can be reported and blocked right in the app. Blocked people's Yos don't
        reach you.</li>
      <li><b>We look within 24 hours.</b> Every report gets a look within a day. Accounts that abuse Yo are removed.
        Yos are end-to-end encrypted, so we can't read them; we go by reports and what we can see, like names.</li>
      <li><b>Apple’s EULA.</b> From the App Store, Apple’s <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">standard
        EULA</a> applies too.</li>
      <li><b>Law.</b> German law applies, without taking away the consumer protections of your own country.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Contact: <a href={`mailto:${operator.email}`}>{operator.email}</a></p>
</section>
